# Step 024 — IMPLEMENT

```step
anchor: IMPLEMENT
touches: [OpticalConstructor.TestWindows, OpticalConstructor.App, OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests]
depends_on: [5, 6, 14, 15, 16, 19, 22, 23]
```

**How to implement.** In TableAndElementRotationView add BayNames.materials with value 'Materials' and BayNames.library with value 'Library' (the samples workbench - the label freed by the step-14 Selector rename) to the BayNames module (:144-156) and mainBays (:1577); thread MaterialProxy and SampleProxy into the host model through initMainWith, updating the composition call mechanically so the solution builds (OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs:125-127; the final WIRE_UI step owns the composition acceptance). Flatten listMaterials/searchMaterials and listSamples/searchSamples results into MaterialsControls / SampleLibraryControls rows and map their Handlers to Msgs exactly as libraryState / flattenNode do for the Selector (TableAndElementRotationView.fs:1012,999). Verbs: the search boxes and facet selectors drive proxy queries; View shows read-only metadata plus the step-19 dual-axis n/k chart for materials and the LayerBandsControls band view over the expanded stack for samples (as the Details bay already renders); Add/Edit open the step-22/23 editor windows; Remove is confirm-gated inline, and a MaterialStillReferenced block surfaces as an inline message naming the referencing samples - never a cascade. Every verb re-queries its proxy so the list refreshes in the same render pass.

**Acceptance.** After the step, headless tests MUST drive both bays end to end by UiIds: search filters the rows, Add/Edit open the editor windows, removing a referenced material surfaces the MaterialStillReferenced message and leaves the store unchanged, and removing an unreferenced entry updates the list in the same render pass.
